   1: # `#529` (crimewidthkill): a guest byte or halfword access to the SGI IP32's CRIME ended the emulator -- declined now and announced once, defended by a 226-row detector whose review chain ran sixteen repairs and closed on repair 16's F2 pass
   2: 
   3: **The defect, witnessed at rung 3.**  `DEVICE_ACCESS(crime)` in `src/devices/dev_sgi_ip32.c` served lengths 4 and 8 and
   4: called `fatal(); exit(1);` on any other, so one guest lb/lbu/lh/lhu/sb/sh anywhere in CRIME (physical 0x14000000) ended
   5: the emulator process.  `regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/crime_width_witness_20260913.py` on the unmodified `-E sgi -e
   6: ip32`: the committed build 3/15 -- every refusal row red, the three controls green (`witness_committed.out`) -- and the
   7: fix 15/15 (`witness_fix.out`).
   8: 
   9: **What ships.**
  10: * `src/devices/dev_sgi_ip32.c` -- unchanged since 2026-09-13 (md5 8c1d1545; `est/` byte-identical; the build trees
  11:   cleared, <OWED-CLEARANCE>).  The width arm DECLINES: one latched announce, `[ crime: unimplemented len=%i at 0x%x --
  12:   declined.  (once) ]`, through a new per-instance `warned` field, then `goto crime_declined` -- the function's common
  13:   tail (the HARDINT restore, the INTSTAT recompute, the read-back, `return 1`) -- past the register switch.  Option-set
  14:   member 3, the `#498` sgi_de shape.
  15: * `regress/crime_width_probe.py` (NEW, 226 rows) -- real guest loads and stores through real address decode and
  16:   `memory_rw` on the unmodified machine, one step at a time; LIVENESS and DEVICE-SIGNATURE controls.  Its module
  17:   docstring is the CONTRACT (clause (e)): every edit it is designed to catch, each measured in a named table, and what it
  18:   discloses.
  19: * `regress/gate_arm.sh` -- gate 14 runs it: parse before score, controls OK, exit 0, rows run / correct / emitted
  20:   pinned at 226, none failed.
  21: * `tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py` -- the probe as a gated DETECTOR (its description said 141 rows and pin 141),
  22:   and <OWED-MANIFEST> MANIFEST lines for the round's preserved instruments and scripts (RESEARCH or TOOL, each described
  23:   by its own docstring); `tools/precommit_check.sh` -- `SCORE_CLAIMS_MANIFEST` 31 -> 32; `tools/pipeline/
  24:   check_score_claims.py` -- the hyphen fix (`scorehyphenfp`, whose ledger row said closed with no commit): HEAD's checker
