FILE bugs529.md
   1: 
   2: ## 2026-09-26 - GXEMUL [087a90]: `#529` crimewidthkill CLOSES; what its review files
   3: 
   4: Evidence: `regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/` -- the panels (durable copies beside each pass), the Opus records, the
   5: dedicated jobs, the flagship rulings (the first-hand 09-25 re-ruling in `rerule_20260925/`; repair 15's pass 2 and
   6: repair 16's F2 adjudication), GPT-6 Astra's confirmations, and every kill table with its PRETABLE.
   7: 
   8: ### `crimectllane` (MED, device) - CRIME_CONTROL acts on the raw value of whatever width reaches the exact label 0x08
   9: 
  10: `dev_sgi_ip32.c`, `DEVICE_ACCESS(crime)`, `case CRIME_CONTROL:` (0x008) matches the EXACT label and acts on the RAW
  11: `idata` of the access that reached it.  So a 32-bit `sw 0x800` to `+0x08` -- the HIGH half of the 64-bit register on this
  12: big-endian machine -- carries bit 11 into `CRIME_CONTROL_HARD_RESET` and stops every CPU, while a 32-bit write to
  13: `+0x0c`, the lane that holds bit 11 and the offset NetBSD 1.6.2 writes (the arm's own TODO says so), falls to the
  14: default arm and does nothing.  MEASURED by `#529`'s pass-1 Opus seat (`crimewidthkill/opus_pass1_20260913/out/
  15: rows_base.out`: `sw CTL+08 0x800` halted, `sw CTL+0c 0x800` did not).  `#529`'s detector USES this defect as a channel
  16: (`sw08 halts`, `sw08 msg ctl`, the `sh08` rows) and says so; a round that fixes the lane owes those rows' re-derivation.
  17: Needs a guest witness of what a real driver writes (the PROM's reboot path; NetBSD's watchdog) before choosing a lane
  18: model.  **Two probe comments and `gate_arm.sh` have called this row "filed" since 2026-09-13; it was filed nowhere until
  19: now** (the resumption dossier found it; the flagship's 09-25 re-ruling listed it).
  20: 
  21: ### `crimebankorder` (LOW, device) - the CRIME prelude writes the bank-control registers contiguously; the header interleaves them
  22: 
  23: The prelude's bank loop writes `d->reg[CRIME_MEM_BANK_CTRL0 / sizeof(uint64_t) + bank]` -- CONTIGUOUS offsets
  24: 0x208..0x240 -- while `src/include/thirdparty/crimereg.h:141-148` defines the bank control registers INTERLEAVED (CTRL0
  25: 0x208, CTRL1 0x218, CTRL2 0x210, CTRL3 0x228, CTRL4 0x220, CTRL5 0x238, CTRL6 0x230, CTRL7 0x248; raised by the codex
  26: pass-1 seat on 2026-09-13, re-read 2026-09-26).  If the header is right, banks 1..7 are reported at the wrong offsets
  27: and a guest sizing memory from them reads the wrong layout.  **But the header is itself suspect:** CTRL7 (0x248) is the
  28: same offset as `CRIME_MEM_REFRESH_CNTR` (`:149`), and no bank register sits at 0x240.  Needs a boot witness (the IP32
  29: PROM's memory report, or NetBSD's or OpenBSD's own sizing) before any edit -- the header, not the code, could be wrong.
  30: `#529`'s `top8 anchor` row pins the model's CURRENT layout and says a round re-ordering the banks owes its
  31: re-derivation.  **Called "filed" in the probe since 2026-09-13; filed nowhere until now.**
  32: 
  33: ### `crimecontroldebt` (LOW, detector) - the seven strengthenings `#529`'s F2 adjudication filed rather than owed
  34: 
  35: The flagship's F2 ruling (`crimewidthkill/repair16_f2_20260926/fable5_f2_adjudication.md`, Q4) closed the chain with NO
  36: row owed and FILED these, each with its measured or derived kill and its re-run cost:
  37: 1. a value anchor BESIDE the prefix count in `ctldog`/`ctlrst` -- kills `D_dogbit0` (226/226 today); re-runs
  38:    `D_nodogclear`'s red set.  (An anchor IN PLACE of the count loses `H_noresetclear`: `opus_f2/replay_ctl.out`.)
  39: 2. a latch-SET `sh 0x0201` in `sh08b` -- kills `P_ctl2wrc_set`; re-runs M8 and M1.
  40: 3. one free-running accepted `sw 0x0001` session -- kills `M_ctldebug` (the arm's `fatal()` demoted to `debug()`, which
  41:    every stepped session prints either way: `opus_f2/disc_f2.out`).
  42: 4. an `lb` appended after the first refusal in the `istat`/`imask` sessions -- kills `W_istlb`/`W_imklb` (226/226,
  43:    table 16, as predicted); re-runs M6 and M7.
  44: 5. six latch-CLEAR first-refusal sessions at INTSTAT/INTMASK -- kill the `C_` variants.
  45: 6. a refused `lb +0x10` while the interrupt line is asserted -- kills `P_istprev_set`.
  46: 7. an `sw 0x0801` last-store session -- the HARD_RESET x bit-0 member of the bit-conditioned family, only if (1) is taken.
  47: All are clause-(e) coverage above the floor (the latch and bit 0 are axes the CONTROL arm does not test; the rest are
  48: joints the decline does not distinguish).  Rank below any live defect in `dev_sgi_ip32.c`.
