18: **X1 (F20, the residue VALUE / bit-conditioned clears) -- UPHOLD "disclosed"; REFINE the disclosure and fix a wrong record.** Bit 0 is a bit of the RELATIONALLY compared residue (`idata != 0`), tested as a case nowhere in the arm; a clear gated on it is a floor cell crossed with one bit of a compared value -- the #549 D1 shape, disclosed even when its consequence is real, because grading by consequence reopens #548. glm/kimi-k3's overturn fails on the rule, and their premise that the value anchor is free is false: an added row changes red sets (D_nodogclear would gain two reds) and owes a re-table -- #462's measured cost. The dedicated grok job is right that F20 names one of three: the same conjunct on HARD_RESET and ENDIANESS is DERIVED to escape (every accepted reset store is exactly 0x0800; both 0x0100 writes have bit 0 clear) -- the disclosure names the family and says which member is built (`D_dogbit0`, 226/226) and which are derived. The row notes "ONE CONTROL text, the twin's" claim a witness the count does not verify (under `D_dogbit0` the one text is 0x201): L4, fixed by wording. The anchor, if ever rowed, sits BESIDE the prefix count (`replay_ctl.out`: an anchored count alone reads 1 under `H_noresetclear`) -- FILED.
