101: a substitute.**
102: 
103: **Measured.** `replay_ctl.out` replays the probe's own sessions from its recorded command lists:
104: 
105:     session         base         H_noresetclear      D_nodogclear       D_dogbit0
106:     ctlrst sw/sd    [0x1]        [0x1, 0x800]        [0x1]              [0x1]
107:     ctldog sw/sd    [0x1]        [0x1]               [0x200, 0x201]     [0x201]
108:     anchored count  1 / 1        ctlrst: 1 (!)       ctldog: 0          ctldog: 0
109: 
110: - **Under `H_noresetclear`,** the count of `control 0x0000000000000001` in `ctlrst` is 1, exactly as on the fixed
111:   build. A `ctlrst` row counting the anchored text instead of the prefix would be green on the round's own L2 cell.
112: - **In `ctldog` it only appears to work.** There the `0x0201` twin carries the DOG bit, so a skipped DOG clear also
113:   changes the twin's value. The `0x0001` twin in `ctlrst` carries no HARD_RESET.
114: - **The aggregate rows have the same trap.** A substituted anchor in `rearm/latch ctl msg` would miss the two extra
115:   `0x100` texts that `E_noendianclear` prints.
