FABLE5_F2ADJ_ALIVE_0926 -- CHECKPOINT.md line 1, verbatim: `# CHECKPOINT -- 2026-09-26 06:35 (087a90 sections rewritten; the peer's sections below are untouched)`

**VERDICT: THE CHAIN CLOSES ON THIS PASS -- zero floor breaches survive adjudication on a valid, full-roster pass; repair 16's rows all stand; NO row is owed. Two of the main loop's GRADES are overturned without moving a row: the latch-gated clears (X3) and the bit-conditioned clears (X1) are both clause (e) -- the CONTROL arm distinguishes neither the latch nor bit 0 -- so the deleted clause-(e) sentence goes back and the "closes the residue-text channel AS A CLASS" heading comes out (it is true of the COUNT for the arm's TESTED bits, false of the value axis and of the print channel). ENDIANESS stays clause (e) and its rows stay as a licensed strengthening. Seven L4 record corrections land in the probe's text before the base leg is re-run on the final bytes; every strengthening named by any seat is FILED, none is in-round. Astra confirms; nothing commits before #549.**
## Where the colleague's draft is wrong or overstated
