**Q1(a).** REASONED: `session()` is `pty.fork()` + `os.execv` per session (READ), so emulator state (regs, `d->warned`, `d->reg[]`, `last_microseconds`) cannot cross. The only physically shared mutable media visible in the packet: (i) the host wall clock - consumed by `crime_update_crime_time`, but per-session baselined by the `last_microseconds == 0` guard plus the one-tick-at-first-step premise (READ), and the channel magnitudes are deliberately 100x separated (SMALL = 6.6M ticks = 100 ms of wall vs. �0.25 s command windows) so load jitter can't flip a `mag()` (REASONED); (ii) the DUMMY image, read-only at load - no session writes files. NOT SETTLEABLE from packet: the semantics of `-V`/`-x` (whether the guest can free-run before the first `step`); the base leg at 218/218 with the one-tick model is consistent with paused start, but if you want it nailed, the settling fact is the flag definitions plus whether `tickshift` arithmetic matches the cited machine.c lines.

