**Q1(c).** TRUE. READ: the REV case tests only `(pc & 0xffffff00) == 0xbfc05100` - no `writeflag` test (the probe's own comment says so), no len test. Arithmetic: `0xbfc05180 & 0xffffff00 = 0xbfc05100` (walked). So once M5's latch-SET suppression lets a narrow op fall through at +0x00 from PROBE_PC, all four ops redirect - including sb/sh (writes store nothing in the else-branch; redirect is their only effect) and `lh`. Empirically closed: M5's actual red set is exactly `rl lb/lh/sb/sh pc` (READ), and the existing `rev pc` rows prove the pc==PROBE_PC+4 baseline on the fix.

