4:## PEER STATE AFTER ITS LAST CHECKPOINT (09-21 15:0x) -- RECONSTRUCTED BY 087a90 FROM ITS TRANSCRIPT, 2026-09-23\n65:## (the peer\'s own section below is its 15:0x state and is left untouched; this note is attribution-marked, not a rewrite)\n77:## GXEMUL (2) [e8a2bc] -- 2026-09-21 15:0x (REPLACED, never appended, by e8a2bc; only up to the next ## header)\n115 _scratchpad/CHECKPOINT.md', 'stderr': '', 'interrupted': False, 'isImage': False, 'noOutputExpected': False}
TRANSCRIPT 287926 2026-09-26T03:00:07.268Z {'type': 'text', 'file': {'filePath': 'C:\\DocumentNoSnc\\cc\\GXEMUL\\_scratchpad\\CHECKPOINT.md', 'content': '# CHECKPOINT -- 2026-09-25 ~21:20 (087a90 sections rewritten; the peer\'s sections below are untouched)\nHEAD: f4f601c4 (#548 fbdrainwire, PRECOMMIT_PASS 0 hard / 8 soft); #547 = bead6ad9; #546 = 3e33201d; #545 = 4264ee20.\n\n## TWO SESSIONS SHARE THIS TREE AND INDEX.  "GXEMUL (2)" [e8a2bc] owns lcalenzerodrop, #530, every dev_lca.c row,\n#540 (lcaisaphys), #541 (alphavmkill), #542 (alphaifetchkill), #544 (cxseatcheck).  This session GXEMUL [087a90]\nowns the footbridge campaign (#545, #548 fbdrainwire), hygienecensus (#546), upstreamdeleteprose (#547), #549\nfbctrlportkill, #550 exemptredate, #551 wdcidselfcheck, the codex farm.\n## INDEX: FREE (no swap in progress; the #548 swap closed md5-verified on 09-24).\n## 087a90 holds UNCOMMITTED records that land with its next commit: regress/pass2_ledger.tsv (the f4f601c4 receipt) and\n##   ledger.json\'s fbdrainwire.commits = f4f601c4.\n## SCRATCH CLONES live OUTSIDE C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL (check_cited_artifacts walks the whole project root): WSL /tmp\n##   or <session scratchpad>.\n## NEXT WEEKLY BATTERY: SUNDAY 2026-09-27 18:00 -- keep the machine quiet from 18:00.\n## BUILD TREES (clearance RUN 2026-09-25 15:42 by <scratchpad>/clear549.sh -- output, not memory): dev_fbctrl.c\n##   part1 CLEAN vs SEC (129694b8) in est/ build/ build-asan/ /tmp/gxsec-build; part2 FRESH in the three build trees\n##   (build/ b5b99e6d, build-asan 1415f934, gxsec-build ec5e6f42); est/ source tree, part 2 N/A; 0 .MUTANT sentinels.\n##   #550/#551 touch only regress/ gates, one regress/ differential and tools/ -- no src/ file.\n## *** CODEX (GPT-6 ASTRA) IS WALLED UNTIL 2026-09-26 07:01 *** -- every codex seat and dedicated job since ~14:14 failed\n##   "usage limit".  RE-FIRE BY HAND after 07:01: the codex seats of the #549 closing / closing-F2 panels and of the\n##   #550 / #551 pass-1 and F2 panels, and the ASTRA adjudications (pointer form, cxlaunch.sh).\n##   OWNER RULING 2026-09-25 (memory gxemul-owner-rulings-20260925): "Fable now, Astra confirms" -- Fable adjudicates\n##   tonight; NOTHING IS COMMITTED until Astra has confirmed.  And #551 = "24/128 now, file the rest".\n\n## 087a90 -- 2026-09-25 ~21:20  ALL THREE ROUNDS READY TO COMMIT; WAITING ONLY ON ASTRA (codex resets 07:01)\n*** IF A commit55x.sh/commit549.sh RUN (--precheck or --go) WAS INTERRUPTED: the working tree may hold committed or\n  HEAD versions of CHANGELOG/OUTSTANDING_BUGS/gate_offline/gate_arm/gate_mips_folds/pass2_ledger/precommit/checker/\n  ledger/matrix.  RESTORE from the newest <scratchpad>/records/bk55x_*/ (MD5.before lists them), then\n  `git reset -q` the staged paths.  The pre-commit HOOK reads the working tree: that is why the scripts swap. ***\n* ALL TOOLING in <scratchpad>/records/ (dry-run OK each): prep550.py + commit550.sh + msg550.txt; prep551.py +\n  commit551.sh + msg551.txt; prep549.py + commit549.sh + msg549.txt; ledger_550_551.py (records550 / records551 <sha550>\n  / astra / sha), ledger_549.py (records / setcommits / astra / sha).  Drafts: changelog550/551/549.md, bugs550/551/549.md.\n  Every commit script REFUSES on an <OWED or <ASTRA placeholder, a DRY stage, a moved HEAD or an unexpected working\n  file; each backs up first and rebuilds the working files (checker/precommit/ledger carry #529\'s and e8a2bc\'s lines).\n* THE MORNING SEQUENCE: (1) after 07:01 fire Astra: `bash GXEMUL-SEC/tools/cxlaunch.sh <brief> <outdir> astra55x`\n  for regress/artifacts/{exemptredate_20260925/final550/astra_confirm_550.md, wdcidselfcheck_20260925/final551g/\n  astra_confirm_551.md, fbctrlportkill_20260924/final549/astra_confirm_549.md}; (2) read each; write records/\n  astraNNN.verdict + astraNNN.ev; fill the 
