trees; est/ part 2 N/A; no .MUTANT.', '+* 21:5x: `bash <scratchpad>/records/morning_astra.sh astra` does step (1) for all three (refuses before 07:01), then', '+  `... seats` does step (5).  Every path both reference was checked to exist; the #550/#551 Astra briefs were', '+  REPOINTED from the superseded bugs550_551.md to bugs550.md / bugs551.md (the files prep55x.py actually stage).', "+* records/receipt549.txt = step (4)'s receipt line, placeholders <SHA549> <DATE> <ASTRA549>.", '+* #529 (NOT before #549 commits): a FRESH Fable seat launched 21:58 to re-rule first-hand the three fallback-written', '+  "Fable" rulings (C3, C5-vs-C4-RA3, repair 14 incl. Q3 + the stop condition); brief p529/fable_rerule_brief.md,', '+  survey p529/resume_dossier.md.  Verify its model with agent_models.py before counting it; Astra confirms after 07:01.', ' ', ' ## 087a90 -- CARRIED FORWARD (still true; do not lose)', ' * NEVER COMMIT: tools/{BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md, CLAUDE.md, PIPELINE.md, panel.sh}, tools/pipeline/{fable_queue.md,']}], 'userModified': False, 'replaceAll': False, 'contentNotInModelContext': True}
TRANSCRIPT 287957 2026-09-26T03:00:36.036Z {'stdout': ' M regress/diff_wdc_identify.c\n M regress/gate_arm.sh\n M regress/gate_hygiene.sh\n M regress/gate_mips_folds.sh\n M regress/gate_offline.sh\n M regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh\n M regress/gdrom_default_probe.py\n M regress/pass2_ledger.tsv\n M regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py\n M regress/sh4_chcr_probe.py\n M src/cpus/cpu_alpha_palcode.c\n M src/devices/dev_fbctrl.c\n M src/devices/dev_lca.c\n M src/devices/dev_pcc2.c\n M src/devices/dev_sgi_ip32.c\n M src/devices/dev_sh4.c\n M src/include/thirdparty/mvme_pcctworeg.h\n M tools/BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md\n M tools/CLAUDE.md\n M tools/PIPELINE.md\n M tools/adjudicate.sh\n M tools/panel.sh\n M tools/pipeline/check_boilerplate.py\n M tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py\n M tools/pipeline/check_score_claims.py\n M tools/pipeline/fable_queue.md\n M tools/pipeline/ledger.json\n M tools/pipeline/matrix.html\n M tools/precommit_check.sh\n----\n1\t0\tregress/pass2_ledger.tsv\n28\t28\ttools/pipeline/ledger.json\n9\t178\ttools/pipeline/matrix.html', 'stderr': '', 'interrupted': False, 'isImage': False, 'noOutputExpected': False}
TRANSCRIPT 287974 2026-09-26T03:00:48.744Z {'stdout': 'diff --git a/regress/gate_hygiene.sh b/regress/gate_hygiene.sh\nindex 193b5054..221ecd71 100644\n--- a/regress/gate_hygiene.sh\n+++ b/regress/gate_hygiene.sh\n@@ -382,7 +382,7 @@ check "readiness: no unrecognised endswith spelling" "$unknown" "$EXPECT_UNKNOWN\n #  and reds THREE rows -- this one, the promptless count and the promptless-names row -- because all three are\n #  grandfathered names that exist only in the working tree (measured on a copy with them removed: 70/73, 40/43,\n #  names gone=the three).  Written by `tools/derive_hygiene_pins.sh --write`, never by hand. ***\n-EXPECT_PTY_PROBES=73\n+EXPECT_PTY_PROBES=74\n #  *** AND THE SAME PROBE BROKE A SECOND CENSUS IN THIS FILE, WHICH pass 11\'s OWN\n #  REPAIR DID NOT FIX.  Found by the codex seat reviewing that repair. ***\n #\n@@ -593,7 +593,7 @@ fi\n #  send() spelled the fresh mark `mark=mark`, which the fresh-mark census does not read, so that one said\n #  23 and the three #392 counts DISAGREED at HEAD.  The probe\'s rename to `_mark` (same change) makes the\n #  three agree; the deriver refuses to write while they disagree, which is why the rename precedes the pin. ***\n-EXPECT_CONVERTED=24\n+EXPECT_CONVERTED=25\n #  One helper for all three, so they agree on WHAT they look at.  The first draft\n #  used py_code() for the anchored count and a raw grep for the other two, which\n #  meant a comment mentioning the echo guard would have inflated one count and not\n regress/diff_wdc_identify.c | 97 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----\n regress/gate_mips_folds.sh  | 77 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n regress/gate_offline.sh     | 57 +++++++++++++++-----------\n src/devices/dev_fbctrl.c    | 23 ++++++++---\n 4 files changed, 215 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)', 'stderr': '', 'interrupted': False, 'isImage': False, 'noOutputExpected': False}
TRANSCRIPT 288056 2026-09-26T03:02:12.343Z {'stdout': 'f4f601c4 #548 fbdrainwire: #442\'s drain probe wired into gate 14 on all four timers before its exemption lapse\nbead6ad9 #547 upstreamdeleteprose: one word of a comment turns gate 8\'s delete row green at HEAD; attrabbrev: \n3e33201d #546 hygienecensus: gate 6\'s readiness census was 24 probes stale and RED at HEAD -- re-derived by a \n4264ee20 #545 fbdeclinefive: five footbridge register accesses the DC21285 does not define ended the process -\nf685d75c records: five "fable5" rulings on record were written by claude-opus-4-8 after a refusal -- corrected\n9c28ca56 #539 receipt: pass-2 receipt for 7836071, gate_arm log and the three-tree propagation clearance filed\n78360718 #539 n6: the footbridge IRQEnable read computed the right value and then ended the process -- the exi\na11eaac4 #538 lcalenzerodrop closes: #530\'s width row pinned one byte lane of four -- all four rowed, 17/17 as\n408accf7 gate 2: SC_EXEMPT\'s two dates had passed on 2026-09-02 with no owner -- re-dated to 2026-09-27 by own\neec0f4a3 #536 wiringcliff: two probes wired into gate_arm.sh, eleven exemptions re-dated to 2026-09-27 by owne\ncdbe7d75 #537 fbsmlane: #442\'s harness printed a verdict token its own self-mutant lane could never read -- th\ne0be9b2a records: #530\'s §F2 pass and the flagship ruling -- one floor breach (the lane axis), not seven; #53\n----\n22286:### `batterymissedruns` (HIGH, harness) — the weekly batteries of 2026-09-06 and 2026-09-13 left no verdict, and nothing said so\n0', 'stderr': '', 'interrupted': False, 'isImage': False, 'returnCodeInterpretation': 'No matches found', 'noOutputExpected': False}
TRANSCRIPT 288132 2026-09-26T03:03:25.161Z {'type': 'text', 'file': {'filePath': 'C:\\DocumentNoSnc\\cc\\GXEMUL\\GXEMUL-SEC\\tools\\BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md', 'content': '# PANEL BRIEF SKELETON — copy this, do not write a brief from memory\n\n**Adopted 2026-08-28 by flagship adjudication.**  Every section below exists because a\nmeasured incident cost this project something, and the reason is recorded with it.  This file\nis the artifact present at the moment a brief is written, which is this project\'s own finding\nabout where prose actually fires:\n\n> *"the premise-audit paragraph is the one piece of prose that demonstrably works ... it lives\n> in the BRIEF TEMPLATE, the artifact present at the moment of decision.  That is structure in\n> the sense that matters — text located where the decision happens, not text located where the\n> reasoning was recorded."*\n\n**THE FAILURE THIS FILE EXISTS TO STOP is not forgetting the rules.  It is remembering them\nand not applying them to the object in front of you.**  The `SETTLED PREMISES` section below\nwas invented on 2026-08-27, applied correctly the same evening at 22:21, and **dropped at\n11:55 the next morning by its own author in the next brief of the same campaign** — fourteen\nhours from minting to breaking.  Nobody had forgotten it.\n\n---\n\n## §A — THE OPENER (copy verbatim, adjust the incident count)\n\n```\n## READ THIS FIRST — PLEASE DO NOT SIMPLY RATIFY\n\nA recent panel had seven of nine seats confirm a premise this brief\'s author stated\nwrongly.  **Check the premises, not just the derivations.**  Where I state something as\nfact, ask whether it is true.  A seat that re-derives a premise from something this brief\ndid NOT give it is worth more than a seat that agrees.\n\n**THE TREE UNDER REVIEW IS `GXEMUL-SEC/src/`.**  There are THREE pristine-2021-upstream\ncopies of GXemul under the project root (`./src/` and two under\n`_archive/audit-results-*/builds/`).  They are NOT this fork.  If your line numbers\ndisagree with mine by hundreds you are reading one of them — say so rather than\nreconciling.\n\n**If you cannot read files that is expected** — every fact you need is inlined.  Name any\npremise you cannot settle from this packet rather than guessing at it.\n\n**Where this brief states an ARITHMETIC claim — an index range, an offset, a count of\nreachable addresses — ENUMERATE it rather than reasoning about it.**  Walk the values.\nA derivation that skips one masking line reads exactly like a correct one.\n\n**And ENUMERATE THE RIGHT DOMAIN — a domain is itself a premise.**  Ask what the PRODUCER of\nthese values can actually emit before you walk them.  Walking every member of a set you have\nnot audited is not enumeration; it is a derivation with more steps, and it reads exactly like\na correct one.\n\n**VERDICT LINE FIRST**, so your answer survives truncation.\n```\n\n**Why each line is here:** the premise-audit instruction has two prior trials and caught\nsomething both times, the second finding FOUR wrong premises.  The tree-naming line exists\nbecause a seat once returned 80 KB of internally-consistent review of the WRONG `src/`.  The\ncannot-read-files line exists because a stalled packet-fed seat is indistinguishable from a\nquota wall in the output, and this project misdiagnosed that for days.  Verdict-line-first\nexists because answers get truncated and the verdict is what survives.\n\n> ### *** THE ENUMERATE-DO-NOT-REASON LINE, ADDED 2026-08-30 ON FIVE MEASURED INSTANCES IN\n> ### ONE EVENING -- TWO OF THEM REFUTATIONS OF THIS PROJECT\'S OWN FILINGS. ***\n>\n> Source-derived arithmetic about *device index expressions* was wrong twice and right three\n> times that night, and **the discriminator every time was enumeration rather than argument**:\n>\n> * `sgilinearoob`\'s *"load-bearing HOST memory safety"* 
TRANSCRIPT 288177 2026-09-26T03:04:12.471Z {'stdout': '26:#  whatever happened to be at the old address, or nothing.  $GXROOT overrides for testing.\n28:ROOT="${GXROOT:-$(cd "$_HERE/../.." && pwd)}"\n29:SEC=$ROOT/GXEMUL-SEC\n#  A green run means the decidable things were checked.  It is not evidence\n#  about correctness. ***\nset -u\n#  ROOT IS DERIVED FROM THIS SCRIPT\'S OWN LOCATION, not hardcoded.  This file lives in\n#  GXEMUL-SEC/tools/, so the project root is two levels up.  It used to carry an absolute\n#  path, which is only half-tracked: a fresh clone anywhere else would have run against\n#  whatever happened to be at the old address, or nothing.  $GXROOT overrides for testing.\n_HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]:-$0}")" && pwd)"\nROOT="${GXROOT:-$(cd "$_HERE/../.." && pwd)}"\nSEC=$ROOT/GXEMUL-SEC\nEST=$ROOT/est\nBLD=$ROOT/build\nMSGFILE=${1:-}\nfail=0\nwarn=0\n\nsay  () { printf \'%s\\n\' "$*"; }\nbad  () { fail=$((fail+1)); printf \'  FAIL  %s\\n\' "$*"; }\nsoft () { warn=$((warn+1)); printf \'  WARN  %s\\n\' "$*"; }\ngood () { printf \'  ok    %s\\n\' "$*"; }\n#  `warn` is called at the four "checker MISSING" branches and was DEFINED NOWHERE -- so a\n#  missing pipeline checker printed `warn: command not found` on stderr and its gate was\n#  silently disabled, which is the exact failure those branches exist to announce.  Measured\n#  by renaming check_stage_panels.py and check_seats_read.py away: both gates vanished and the\n#  run still said PRECOMMIT_PASS.\nwarn () { soft "$@"; }\n\ncd "$SEC" || { say "no repo at $SEC"; exit 9; }\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- F\n#  THE PASS-2 RECEIPT, AND THIS IS THE SECOND VERSION BECAUSE THE FIRST COULD NOT FIRE.\n#\n#  R6 shipped without a pass-2 review of its diff.  That was caught externally,\n#  recorded, and corrected -- and R7 then did exactly the same thing one round\n#  later.  So a mechanical check was written.  A pass-2 seat then MEASURED that\n#  the check itself was vacuous: it sat below the "nothing staged" early exit, so\n#  on a clean post-commit tree -- the only state in which a missed pass 2 is\n#  actually detectable -- the script returned before reaching it.  It also keyed\n#  on source mtime, which any checkout or copy moves, and accepted any panel\n#  directory as evidence without asking what that panel reviewed.\n#\n#  A check that cannot fail is worse than no check, because it reassures.  This\nset -u\nHERE=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)\nROOT=$(cd "$HERE/.." && pwd)\nHOOK="$ROOT/.git/hooks/pre-commit"\nif [ ! -d "$ROOT/.git" ]; then\n    echo "install_hooks: $ROOT is not a git working tree" >&2\n    exit 1\nfi\nmkdir -p "$ROOT/.git/hooks"\nif [ -e "$HOOK" ] && ! grep -q "precommit_check.sh" "$HOOK" 2>/dev/null; then\n    if [ "${1:-}" != "--force" ]; then\n        echo "install_hooks: $HOOK exists and is NOT ours -- refusing to clobber." >&2\n        echo "               re-run with --force if you mean to replace it." >&2\n        exit 1\n    fi\n#!/bin/bash\n#  Installed by tools/install_hooks.sh -- do not edit here; edit the installer.\n#  Runs the full precommit gate and BLOCKS the commit if it is red.\nROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\nOUT=$(mktemp)\nbash "$ROOT/tools/precommit_check.sh" > "$OUT" 2>&1\nrc=$?\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\n    echo "" >&2\n    echo "=========================================================" >&2\n    echo "  COMMIT BLOCKED -- precommit_check.sh is RED." >&2\n    echo "=========================================================" >&2\n    grep -E \'^  FAIL|^  WARN|PRECOMMIT_\' "$OUT" >&2\n    echo "" >&2\n    echo "  full output: $OUT" >&2\n    echo "  to bypass deliberately:  git commit --no-verify" >&2\n    exit 1\nfi\ngrep -E \'PRECOMMIT_\' "$OUT"\nrm -f "$OUT"', 'stderr': '', 'interrupted': False, 'isImage': False, 'noOut
TRANSCRIPT 288202 2026-09-26T03:04:35.486Z {'stdout': '\tif wslout=$(python "$SEC/tools/pipeline/check_wsl_dollar.py" "$SEC" 2>&1); then\n\t\tgood "$(printf "%s" "$wslout" | sed -e "s/^ *//" | head -1)"\n\telse\n\t\tprintf "%s\\n" "$wslout" | while IFS= read -r l; do bad "$l"; done\n\t\tfail=$((fail+1))\n\tfi\nelse\n\tbad "check_wsl_dollar.py MISSING -- section Z proved nothing"\n\tfail=$((fail+1))\nfi\n\nif [ -z "$CHANGED" ]; then\n\tsay "nothing staged or modified -- no per-file checks."\n\t#  *** DO NOT exit 0 HERE.  *** Sections F/G/H/I/J/K have already run above and may have\n\t#  set `fail`.  The old form discarded them: measured on a clean tree with a stale carrier\n\t#  and a missing pass-2 receipt, it printed SIX `FAIL` lines, no verdict line at all, and\n\t#  exited 0.  A clean tree is precisely the state in which those checks are meaningful --\n\t#  F was deliberately moved above this exit for that reason, and then the exit threw its\n\t#  answer away.\n\tif [ $fail -gt 0 ]; then\n\t\tsay ""\n\t\tsay "=========================================================="\n\t\tsay "PRECOMMIT_FAIL   $fail hard, $warn soft"\n\t\texit 1\n\tfi\n\tsay "PRECOMMIT_PASS   0 hard, $warn soft"\n\texit 0\nfi\n\nsay "=== #418-era PRE-COMMIT REWORK CHECK ==="\nsay "files in play:"; printf \'    %s\\n\' $CHANGED\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- A\n#  TWIN-TREE PROPAGATION.  est/ and GXEMUL-SEC differ by exactly five named\n#  files plus SEC-only dev_ne2000.c; ANY OTHER src/ file must land byte-\n#  identical in both.  #415 is a whole commit that exists because this was\n#  skipped once -- and the gate that should have caught it named two files when\n#  the truth was three, because an allowlist entry had gone stale.', 'stderr': '', 'interrupted': False, 'isImage': False, 'noOutputExpected': False}
