## Q1. Enumeration audit

**Count of ACCEPTS.** 43 kinds, matches the brief. ✓

**Kind the function can take that ACCEPTS omits.** `ldP` — an 8-byte read from the
PROM-probe window at CRIME_REV (PC 0xbfc05180). ACCEPTS has `lwP` (4R from window)
and `swP`/`sdP` (writes from window); the brief explicitly says the pc test ignores
direction, so `lwP` covers read and `swP` covers write. But `ldP` is a distinct
accepted kind: a mutant that distinguishes 8-byte from 4-byte reads at REV in the
window would not be caught by `lwP` alone. In practice no mutant in the table does
so,
